From 0657ab3282a564abdbeb69ac2a67ec77e9a8ea89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:35:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kboot: Initialize the DAPFs on T8132

DAPF init was skipped on T8132 because it raised an SError. With each
DAPF found from the ADT and its device powered, the full set
initializes.

Without the MTP's DAPF, its DART reports a SID exception as soon as the
MTP starts and RTKit never gets a HELLO, so the keyboard and trackpad
stay dead.

Assisted-By: LLM
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 src/kboot.c | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kboot.c b/src/kboot.c
index ee623d6..bbd6503 100644
--- a/src/kboot.c
+++ b/src/kboot.c
@@ -2907,9 +2907,7 @@ int kboot_boot(void *kernel)
 
     usb_init();
     pcie_init();
-    /* HACK: DAPF init raises an SError on T8132. */
-    if (chip_id != T8132)
-        dapf_init_all();
+    dapf_init_all();
 
     printf("Setting SMP mode to WFE...\n");
     smp_set_wfe_mode(true);
